Mitcad patch (mitcad#441): a fillet contour goes on into an edge asked for
whose faces OCCT takes for tangent but which meet at more than the angular
tolerance.

ChFi3d::IsTangentFaces takes faces up to 0.1 rad apart for tangent. Patch
0022 rounds such an edge where a contour starts from it, when its faces are
farther apart than the angular tolerance (MinNormalAngle). A contour coming
to it from an edge before it stopped there, though: FaceTangency takes the
next edge only when its faces meet at an angle. The edge then started a
contour of its own, whose walks took the edges before it again from the
other side: two stripes over the same edges, which met at no corner (a
thread's chamfer cone rounded along its five edges, the last of them, down
to the root, between faces 0.03 rad apart). FaceTangency now takes such an
edge as one at an angle where it is one of the edges asked for
(StopChainsAtTurns) and its faces meet at more than the angular tolerance;
without StopChainsAtTurns nothing changes.

